{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy","id":1490295,"title":"The economics of Necromancy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-15T14:26:00-07:00","id":1490295,"title":"The economics of Necromancy","content":"The Giovanni Clan has built its power on the capacity to interact with the Shadowlands, to the point of enslaving thousands and thousands of Wraiths, actively plotting to undermine the barrier between worlds and accepting to refrain from active participation in the Jyhad in exchange for being left alone in their necromantic pursuits. <br /> <br /> So, this makes me think that, as the Giovanni are a collection of merchant families, they probably would have found countless ways of monetizing the Shadowlands, to the point of probably creating a whole economic network around them. <br /> <br /> Would the Giovanni create a &quot;colonial economy&quot; in the Shadowlands? And perhaps create &quot;settler societies&quot; of enterprising and alienated necromancers for whom the Shadowlands are the main centre of interest? <br /> <br /> Would they use undead labor in their more despicable factories? Would the Giovanni use their Paths to bring in this world the wraithly remains of lost treasures or powerful soulforged artifacts? <br /> <br /> What do you think? What form would the Giovanni shadow empire take ? How could their necromantic skills be leveraged to keep the Family powerful and affluent in Mortal, Cainite and Wraith society?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T18:31:25-07:00","id":1490328,"title":"","content":"The Giovanni are one of those parts of V:tM that really show the extent of retcon-itis that went on over the years.<br /> <br /> Are the Antedeluvians a myth or are they in deep torpor and will awaken and eat us all? Um, the Giovanni have an active 3rd Generation who is taking business meetings and doesn't seem to eat everyone, not to mention puts to rest the concept of low generation elder existing or not.<br /> <br /> The only thing that can counter ghosts is necromancy. Doesn't that make the Giovanni almost unbeatable then as far as power and being information brokers? Um, well, there is a massive storm in the Underworld that destroys the Giovannis necromantic power build up.<br /> <br /> The Tremere are utterly hated for eaten an Antediluvian, for the Giovanni it was Tuesday. I mean other than the Samedi and Harbingers of Skulls, does anyone really care about Cappadocious getting eaten?<br /> <br /> Every clan is pulled into the great jyhad, except the Giovanni who are just left alone.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue are the greatest vampire bankers and CEO types, the Giovanni have entered chat and now own all the banks that the Ventrue work at.<br /> <br /> The Tremere are deeply distrusted because they partially blood bond new members to the council of seven. The Giovanni ghoul their own mortal family members, then make them essentially earn the embrace through competence and devotion, but they make sure that no one can build a power block by mixing who embraces who. The Giovanni family is really the Tremere Pyramid 2.0 with better marketing.<br /> <br /> So the fact that the entire Shadowlands side of the Giovanni empire never being fleshed out isn't surprising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T20:13:03-07:00","id":1490344,"title":"","content":"The Giovanni clan is one of those concepts that I feel many people are portraying &quot;wrong&quot; in their chronicles. People make them far larger and more powerful than I think they should be. No problems if that is what you want in your chronicles, but I don't think it's the best design choice. And I don't portray the Giovanni clan like that in my own chronicles.<br /> <br /> First, as originally written, the Giovanni were a rather small clan. They were limited to making no more than 3 vampires every generation, which is about once a decade. Which means they have embraced only around 50 new vampires since the Promise of 1528 plus whatever number they had before then. As originally written, there is probably less than a hundred. I know subsequent mentions of the Giovanni dropped this and never mentioned it again, but a clan whose concept is &quot;we only embraced within the family&quot; has to be small. I blame the original Giovanni clanbook for this. It did a good job introducing some more concepts and additional families married into the clan to provide some needed diversity, but grossly overestimated how many vampires these sub-families could actually have. It's actually best to see most of these other families (especially the ones not from Italy who represent Giovanni interests elsewhere) as only having a few vampires at best, maybe half a dozen, with some of the other Italian families having a dozen or so.<br /> <br /> Second, the Giovanni are certainly rich and well off, especially for their small number. But they can't possibly have anywhere near the influence and resources of the Ventrue, and probably many other clans collectively like the Toreador and Tremere. Venice isn't Europe's leading economy and hasn't been for centuries. A clan based out of there and whose wealth is tried to the old Venetian trading networks simply can't surpass clans who operate in all of today's leading economic and financial powers. I view the Giovanni's wealth as being like a hornet's nest. Other vampires leave it alone because it is a hard target, and any benefit they would get from raiding it or attempting to destroy it just isn't worth their cost. The Giovanni can't compete with the influence of most of the Camarilla clans, but that is OK because they don't need to. They just need to enjoy enough resources and influences that they can go about their business and not have others meddle with them.<br /> <br /> Third, Vampire has always consistently failed to demonstrate how hostile the Underworld should be to the Giovanni. Vampire acts like there aren't any other competitors for them, or dangerous factions they would need to avoid. And that's completely false. The Hierarchy is dangerous. And even individual groups of Heretics and Renegades can also be dangerous in local conditions. The Giovanni simply can't enslave any ghosts they want. They need to tread carefully and not upset the other powers. Vampire has always treated the other spirit worlds fairly badly despite having several concepts that show there is a small, but active, group of vampires who do involve themselves in it. Because Vampire supports those kinds of games very poorly, an ST either needs to master an entire new game line, put tremendous individual effort into figuring things out in their own chronicles, or just leave it blank and let PCs and NPCs do whatever they like. Let's say you are an ST who wants to run a Giovanni centric game, or provide a lot of individual feedback to his gaming group, one of whom plays a Giovanni PC. What is more interesting? Just letting the Giovanni do whatever they like, or running a rich setting where they have to actually navigate obstacles, politics, and rivals? The Necromancy powers of the Giovanni should make them a hard target for Wraiths, and if they behave within reason they can get by and advance their plot. But they can't run roughshod over Wraiths. Again, I blame the clanbooks here. Because they are written in character, there is a lot of bluster about how powerful and feared the Giovanni are in the Shadowlands. But that has to be taken with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> So I see the Giovanni as a relatively small clan with minor absolute power compared to the big sects. However, they do punch way above their weight. And in the relatively small areas where they do have interests, they are major players. Over all, they don't control the world economy. But you'd be a fool to try something in Venice or a dozen other cities where they have major interests.<br /> <br /> In the Shadowlands, their power is mostly contained. In terms of their influence there, they are at best like a large criminal gang or minor warlord in certain Necropoli, and absent almost everywhere else. They are just enough of a factor to make deals with certain other small, local political factions, but not too large that they'd attract attention as a potential threat and crushed like a bug. Their Necromancy can wield a lot of power over one or a few wraiths, but anything more and they'd be smacked down. So Giovanni have to be smart, keep a low profile in most circumstances, and avoid open conflicts. Most of their captured wraiths are from their own family, those stupid enough to deal with them, some smart trading of favors with the powers of the Underworld, and some discrete opportunistic captures. And ghostly souls are useful only to them as necromancers. You can't monetize them anywhere else other than the Shadowlands. They are just useless in the real world.<br /> <br /> At best, you might be able to find some lost real world treasures whose locations are forgotten, but which certain wraiths might know (where is the buried treasure of X that has been lost this past four centuries?) A more useful solution would be to use information gathered from wraiths that would help them in their business dealings - raising the spirit of a recently deceased competitor and forcing them to divulge trade secrets would provide them an edge. Or use enslaved wraiths to torment some of their rivals so they end up making mistakes.<br /> <br /> (I find the idea of the Giovanni capturing whatever ridiculous number of souls for their grand experiment to be something that only has value in a chronicle where Gehenna/Apocalypse/Doomsday is near. That was meant to be yet another sign that Gehenna was imminent. If that isn't the chronicle you are running, there is no reason for the Giovanni to be anywhere close to that. And if you follow the V5 line where the Giovanni were basically humbled and the Cappadocians have reclaimed control of their bloodline (albeit calling themselves Hecata now), it is even more superfluous. I don't put much stock in that as a setting concept.)<br /> <br /> In terms of an undead work force? The simple fact is that zombies can only provide mindless labor. They can't do anything value added. In an earlier time, they could use them on plantations and other unskilled tasks. The depiction of Legendre's sugar cane mill in White Zombie makes for a good, evocative image. No reason not to use it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AdspUvlsQrY\" data-code=\"AdspUvlsQrY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/AdspUvlsQrY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> That would be fine during the era of colonial plantations in the 16th to 18th centuries. It'd be very bad now. But something like that may still be done in a few isolated locations in the undeveloped world. But it doesn't generate anything like the old wealth it used to do.<br /> <br /> In my own chronicles, I portray the Giovanni divided between those who seek power in the mortal world, and those who concentrate on the occult. There are not that many Giovanni who crossover and do both because the one aspect takes them too far away from what they are really interested in. That is one of the tensions within the clan in order to make things more interesting from a roleplaying perspective. If you are trying to understand the mysteries of the Labyrinth, contact one of the Far Shores, negotiate with an Anacreon, and so on, you don't want to be bothered with stuff like increasing your bank account. And vice versa.<br /> <br /> That's how I run it at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  fix typo 08-17-2022, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T23:47:42-07:00","id":1490354,"title":"","content":"The weird thing about vampire clan/bloodline size and populations is that things get quite messed up with human population adjustments.<br /> <br /> In previous editions, the 1 to 100,000 mortal ratio included the Kuei-jin population in with the Cainite population for a total Vampire population. So, most Cainite numbers are technically lower than we think of them as. Furthermore, back in 1800 the human population of the world was considered to be only 1 billion strong.<br /> <br /> That would work out to a total vampire population in 1800 of about 10,000, with only 2/3rds of that being Cainite. So that works out to be about 6,666 Cainites in total who are active, in torpor, or in other dimensions. Now divide that by 13 Clans and you have about 500 members per clan and the leftovers covering the Bloodlines. So, for the Giovanni numbers would be only slightly smaller than other clans.<br /> <br /> Of course, with our current population which is supposed to hit 8 billion by November of this year, that would mean a vampire population cap of around 80,000 blood suckers, and a Cainite population of around 53,333 or so. Thus, you could take whatever Giovanni clan number you had in 1800 and multiply it by 9 and still be under pop-cap for the modern nights.<br /> <br /> This is of course not touching on the fact that the Giovanni, Cappadocians, Harbingers of Skulls, and the Samedi are all one big mess when it comes to categorization and family trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T01:03:23-07:00","id":1490356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy#post1490295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this makes me think that, as the Giovanni are a collection of merchant families, they probably would have found countless ways of monetizing the Shadowlands, to the point of probably creating a whole economic network around them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490328#post1490328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that can counter ghosts is necromancy. Doesn't that make the Giovanni almost unbeatable then as far as power and being information brokers?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a small section in Ghost Hunters where a guy from the Syndicate brags about their cool plan for establishing economic relations with the Hierarchy built on common interests; you know, keep Wraiths out of the Skinlands, transfer some Artifacts, safeguard Fetters, cozy afterlife in return for favors etc. The Giovanni could have easily set up similar deals, although I think their approach would be more aggressive. Organized crime works in the Shadowlands just as well as it does in the Skinlands, but I have no doubt they also have some Hierarchy higher-ups in their pocket.<br /> <br /> Having said that, in my opinion having access to Wraiths is far more useful on this side of the Shroud. Corporate espionage is trivial with invisible, incorporeal agents- some of which can even possess machines and siphon data or sabotage them. Same for market manipulation. But as the above example shows, there's competition. Once you get into the big league, you have competing supernaturals everywhere.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T02:44:26-07:00","id":1490361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490328#post1490328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere are utterly hated for eaten an Antediluvian, for the Giovanni it was Tuesday. I mean other than the Samedi and Harbingers of Skulls, does anyone really care about Cappadocious getting eaten?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well technically they diablerised their own Antediluvian, just like the Brujah, and allegedly the Lasombra and Tzimisce. They then became the main line of their own clan. So they're not quite the same as the Tremere, who were never vampires to begin with, and then stole vampirism, and completely replaced a clan that they were unrelated to.<br /> <br /> Augustus Giovanni diablerising Cappadocius is just like Troile diablerising Brujah, only more recently, and with the Camarilla turning a blind eye as they purge the old remnants of the clan.<br /> <br /> There's probably a different set of in-character attitudes to bloodlines that takeover their parent clans and become the 'main' line than there is to pretenders who usurp an unrelated line altogether. (You might even argue that the Nosferatu fall into this group, too, bringing the total number of clans who've allegedly done this to at least three.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 08-16-2022, 05:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T03:49:33-07:00","id":1490364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490356#post1490356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a small section in Ghost Hunters where a guy from the Syndicate brags about their cool plan for establishing economic relations with the Hierarchy built on common interests; you know, keep Wraiths out of the Skinlands, transfer some Artifacts, safeguard Fetters, cozy afterlife in return for favors etc. The Giovanni could have easily set up similar deals, although I think their approach would be more aggressive. Organized crime works in the Shadowlands just as well as it does in the Skinlands, but I have no doubt they also have some Hierarchy higher-ups in their pocket.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my games the Giovanni operate as a neutral group in the Shadowlands. They're powerful enough nobody really wants to mess with them, so they can do what they want within reason. They serve as a &quot;neutral ground&quot; for meetings for wraiths from various Dark Kingdoms. They also offer sanctuary to Renegades or members of Guilds who find the Hierarchy after them. As a neutral party they tend to do a lot of trading and bartering with various wraiths and Dark Kingdoms. Several Giovanni strongholds are also warded and serve as places of respite in the Tempest so wraiths who are travelling with often end up staying with the Giovanni for a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T07:02:14-07:00","id":1490384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490354#post1490354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In previous editions, the 1 to 100,000 mortal ratio included the Kuei-jin population in with the Cainite population for a total Vampire population. So, most Cainite numbers are technically lower than we think of them as. Furthermore, back in 1800 the human population of the world was considered to be only 1 billion strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>For whatever it is worth, I must point out that the 1:100.000 ratio is modern, and we're not given historical rates. So while this was true in the 90's, probably the 80's, we can safely assume higher vampire ratios as we go back in time.<br /> <br /> And if we take the DA books at face value, the Cappadocians that attended the Feast of Folly were 12 thousand strong. While they were the most numerous clan by a large margin (and that was kind of the point), that does indicate that vampire society at the time wouldn't find it too incredible that their global numbers were something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T12:15:44-07:00","id":1490420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490356#post1490356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Corporate espionage is trivial with invisible, incorporeal agents- some of which can even possess machines and siphon data or sabotage them. Same for market manipulation. But as the above example shows, there's competition. Once you get into the big league, you have competing supernaturals everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of those things that sounds great on paper until you try to map it out mechanically. When you look at a character sheet, business really is a matter of Backgrounds rather than stats or disciplines. Focusing on Dominate until level three gets the best results for generating Background dots and rank five Resources can be taken at character generation quite cheaply if you want a head start on things.<br /> <br /> But then what do you do exactly? Resources is capped at five dots, unless you are pooling your background dots with your Coterie, but even then, there is very little difference in game play between Resources 5 and Resources 25 when you are buying something small like a house or a luxury car. So you start buying things like businesses or corporations, but what exactly do you do with them?<br /> <br /> Owning a private military company gives you access to military grade weaponry and mercenaries on command, but most of the time that is too blatant to be of use in first world countries. Sinking the money into science or research doesn't really work since the game breaks if you make changes to the setting. A clone blood supply upends most of the drama and breaks the need for several game systems. Creating a bioweapon like in Seraph of the End to allow for vampire supremacy likewise up ends things. <br /> <br /> So while I agree that Necromancy and ghostly minions can help generate Background dots and are useful, the weird thing is that once you get to a certain point you suffer from diminishing returns. Once you have maxed out the business-related Backgrounds, what exactly is the benefit? So far the only thing I can think of is the potential to have full access to your Backgrounds in more varied story scenarios, but that is an ST thing rather than a mechanical one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T12:55:42-07:00","id":1490428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490420#post1490420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then what do you do exactly? Resources is capped at five dots, unless you are pooling your background dots with your Coterie, but even then, there is very little difference in game play between Resources 5 and Resources 25 when you are buying something small like a house or a luxury car. So you start buying things like businesses or corporations, but what exactly do you do with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Jeff Bezos doesn't need any more money either, but that doesn't stop him from making more. Money is only a medium for power anyways, especially for vampires. You put those resources into influence, into your Clan, the mortal world, or into buying blood dolls for your favorite elder. Or if you're really good, buy the elder to lower your generation. Anything to have the longer lever in case somebody tries to flick you off the board.<br /> There is no end game to this. Vampires are incredibly selfish, paranoid creatures and have an infinite unlife to protect.<br /> <br /> Like you said, this is more of a narrative process than a mechanical one, but there is no difference in this and other tools vampires use to get on top of the pecking order. Necromancy maybe has the unique advantage that you can arrange for second round in the Shadowlands in case somebody in the Skinlands manages to destroy you.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T16:25:36-07:00","id":1490453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490428#post1490428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Jeff Bezos doesn't need any more money either, but that doesn't stop him from making more. Money is only a medium for power anyways, especially for vampires. You put those resources into influence, into your Clan, the mortal world, or into buying blood dolls for your favorite elder. Or if you're really good, buy the elder to lower your generation. Anything to have the longer lever in case somebody tries to flick you off the board.<br /> There is no end game to this. Vampires are incredibly selfish, paranoid creatures and have an infinite unlife to protect.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the examples you gave are kind of off the mark regarding what I am talking about.<br /> <br /> A Resources 5 vampire will behave differently than most street level vampires. They will have havens spread across the country, if not the world. Chances are that a few of them will be retrofitted decommissioned military sites that have been upgraded to meet supernatural defense standards. These hardened sites are usually outside of normal cities and thus not under the rule of a Prince. Thanks to the internet you can run your entire empire from that hardened bunker complex. Furthermore, you can keep a private herd there with little effort or security risk.<br /> <br /> Now that your shelter, food supply, and means of maintaining power (Resources, Influence, Contacts, Allies) are taken care of, then what? The more secure your own existence becomes, the less &quot;game&quot; there is to play. If there is a struggle between factions in a given city, what do you care since you exist outside of that city even if you may own a business or three located there?<br /> <br /> Yes money is a tool, and having more money just gives you more options for how to use it, but at the same time there is a ceiling to what you are allowed to achieve in the game system because most WoD splats are not expected to be able to change the world. Exalted on the other hand are expected to change history simply by existing and the setting/mechanics are written accordingly.<br /> <br /> Building up power in the underworld doesn't translate in general terms to the living realms. Sure you can ghostly minions or spies, you could potentially recover lost information from people who took their secrets to their graves. But you can't take an Underworld resource and go to vegas with it. Likewise you can't take a stack of hundred dollar bills or a flash card with a bitcoin account on it and try to buy something in the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T18:35:57-07:00","id":1490468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490420#post1490420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while I agree that Necromancy and ghostly minions can help generate Background dots and are useful, the weird thing is that once you get to a certain point you suffer from diminishing returns. Once you have maxed out the business-related Backgrounds, what exactly is the benefit? So far the only thing I can think of is the potential to have full access to your Backgrounds in more varied story scenarios, but that is an ST thing rather than a mechanical one.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I do agree with you in that the system isn't made to deal with this style of play (corporate-style conflicts), there are two points to consider.<br /> <br /> First, while we're discussing the clan, the benefits for the character aren't so much the point as the benefits for the clan, which is a story element, not a mechanical element. The clan has every reason to want that edge, and the character works fine as the provider of such strategy for the clan even if the game has no mechanic for them to benefit themselves.<br /> <br /> But also, at least since the V20 Companion, the game <i>does</i> have a way to do so: Prestation. The rules on Prestation, while I don't think they should be the one true answer to vampire economics as some people think, works well enough to include such elements in the game as they give mechanical benefits for the tangible descriptions of your resources (both upper and lower case).<br /> <br /> So what a businessman with ghosts infiltrated in their competition can do? They can turn this asset into favors (and ways to pressure people into needing their favors). Favors are the high-end currency the character can now invest on, but also incur as they start to step on the schemes of other vampires. With a little tweak the system can even cover cross-splat relations at this level as they cross paths with other supernatural millionaires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T19:39:46-07:00","id":1490478,"title":"","content":"You have to consider that there are many more wraiths than vampires. If every vampire in the world were a Giovanni, they will still be in a huge numerical disadvantage. <br /> When you add that wraiths also have arcanoi, it's just impossible for the Giovanni to brute force an empire in the Shadwlands, no matter how much some Revised authors wanted to make you believe so. <br /> <br /> The way I see, Necromancy would allow them to bully small fish, but not to play in the Underworld big leagues. If they are clever, and very strong, they could ally with a local faction and make a good profit out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T20:54:19-07:00","id":1490482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490468#post1490468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, while we're discussing the clan, the benefits for the character aren't so much the point as the benefits for the clan, which is a story element, not a mechanical element. The clan has every reason to want that edge, and the character works fine as the provider of such strategy for the clan even if the game has no mechanic for them to benefit themselves.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Clan is one of those things that is and isn't at the same time and the fluff leaves it ambiguous so that people can run the games however they want. To use a concept from Babylon 5 Psi-Corps, The Clan is Mother, The Clan is Father, then of course the random clan member will do what they can to further the Clan agenda because they know the Clan will look out for them in turn. But most of the Clans in V:tM are either shattered or so badly fractured that there is no cohesive vision or agenda. Then half the fluff suggests that ones own clan mates are almost as big a threat as other clan vampires.<br /> <br /> In such an environment while I can see Clan solidarity, blind Clan loyalty is going to be rare, if not ridiculed outside of the regimented clans like Tremere, Giovanni, Followers of Set, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490468#post1490468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But also, at least since the V20 Companion, the game <i>does</i> have a way to do so: Prestation. The rules on Prestation, while I don't think they should be the one true answer to vampire economics as some people think, works well enough to include such elements in the game as they give mechanical benefits for the tangible descriptions of your resources (both upper and lower case).\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I had to reread Prestation, and yep, it gave me a headache now just like it did back then.<br /> <br /> I have played around with &quot;Boon-Generator&quot; character builds for a long time, so working in owed debts is old hat to me. The entire prestation system is a big floating &quot;it works this way because we said so&quot; mechanic, rather than actually thinking about how that would work.<br /> <br /> The part about the Harpies somehow acting as Boon accountants is especially laughable. A large city would have fewer than a dozen vampires in total, like two or three coteries in total, there aren't enough vampires to have Harpies or most court positions be a thing. This also means that Boons are only enforceable if made public knowledge, but if they have to be public knowledge, why not make a proper setup for it, even if it is as cheesy as the John Wick blood thumbprint medallion plot mechanic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490468#post1490468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what a businessman with ghosts infiltrated in their competition can do? They can turn this asset into favors (and ways to pressure people into needing their favors). Favors are the high-end currency the character can now invest on, but also incur as they start to step on the schemes of other vampires. With a little tweak the system can even cover cross-splat relations at this level as they cross paths with other supernatural millionaires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that a cross-splat system of favors could work quite nicely, I feel that is a role play thing rather than a mechanical thing because there is no aspect of oversight for said favors. There is a reason business/contract law is such a big thing IRL, because just saying someone has an IOU doesn't really mean much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T23:28:08-07:00","id":1490487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490482#post1490482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In such an environment while I can see Clan solidarity, blind Clan loyalty is going to be rare, if not ridiculed outside of the regimented clans like Tremere, Giovanni, Followers of Set, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still the Giovanni <b>are</b> one of those clans.<br /> <br /> Also, I din't said it would be for solidarity. My work at a big financial corporation brings dividends to the bank. But I don't do my work out of solidarity with a bank, I do it because the bank pays me or for other benefits I can get within the company.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490482#post1490482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had to reread Prestation, and yep, it gave me a headache now just like it did back then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know how you feel and I find the whole idea of Official Prestation Bookkeeping equally laughable.<br /> <br /> But the core of the system, while poor as is expected from a mechanic created almost overnight as a patch to the setting, does the job. It doesn't make anything really unthinkable happen at the game, but it does give basic tools for the ST to keep track of who owns who and what they can expect out of the deal.<br /> <br /> As an in-game concept it is badly made, but as a tool for the ST and players to visualize this sort of trades, it serves its purpose. And in this specific context, it does give a mechanic to convert and bank narrative benefits the game has no other means to work with.<br /> <br /> Otherwise the fact remains that the character going the extra-mile has actual assets to benefit from, but then we would go back to the state where you and me can manage that because we individually have experience doing this kind of stuff beyond the limits of the system, but the system itself would offer no common ground for us to meaningfully discuss, much less help other players/STs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490482#post1490482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that a cross-splat system of favors could work quite nicely, I feel that is a role play thing rather than a mechanical thing because there is no aspect of oversight for said favors. There is a reason business/contract law is such a big thing IRL, because just saying someone has an IOU doesn't really mean much.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a sense the Prestation mechanics are an attempt at creating a form of Contract Law within the setting. But regardless of its faults, I think that just brushing aside the ridiculous Harpies/Chancellor system it works well as a notation basis out-of-character. And it works across splats or within them.<br /> <br /> Of course, in-character things are muddier. Spoken promises do work in some contexts, among some people, and actually work well most of the time. Of course, you only need one failure if the system doesn't have some sort of self-regulation between the parties. And an actual contract brings the need for external oversight, someone or something that can ensure it's biding powers.<br /> <br /> But the rules as presented already have the tools to make something and put it to work for spoken agreements, and the supernatural splats have their own means to empower contracts if they want to, which most of the time would be the only way to ensure oversight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T01:15:29-07:00","id":1490492,"title":"","content":"I replied earlier but the post seems to have gone missing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490328#post1490328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are the Antedeluvians a myth or are they in deep torpor and will awaken and eat us all? Um, the Giovanni have an active 3rd Generation who is taking business meetings and doesn't seem to eat everyone, not to mention puts to rest the concept of low generation elder existing or not.</div> </div> </div> </div> In short: 3rd gens =/= Antideluvians. Don't forget that Gratiano (ate lasombra) is also active and belived to be 3rd gen. Lugoj is... well, that's actually Tzmisce, but he's the monster we expect from Gehenna. Augustus, Gratiano and Tremere are all 1000 years old. It's doubtful they can capitalize on the power of their blood. They're like sports cars in a 60 zone. Too young to have really fostered world ending power or the alien mindset of a true ancient. The &quot;real&quot; antideluvians that people fear are far, far older monsters who actually have unlocked much of the terrifying potential of their potent blood. Some believe the name is literal and they really did survive God's flood to purge prehistoric evil. A 4th gen of 2000 years is scarier than a 2nd gen of 1000 years. Generation dictates potential, not power in of itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only thing that can counter ghosts is necromancy. Doesn't that make the Giovanni almost unbeatable then as far as power and being information brokers? Um, well, there is a massive storm in the Underworld that destroys the Giovannis necromantic power build up. </div> </div> </div>First, ghosts aren't super reliable and have their own limitations.<br /> Second, Auspex can find ghosts and aid in finding fetters. You don't need necromancy to beat necromancy. Thaumaturgy soundly counters necromancy.<br /> Lastly, and most importantly, most Princes would view ghostly spies violating the recognized Domains of others in an extremely negative manner. Fear of such intrusions would drive more extreme ruling against the necromancer. So unless the bridge has already been burnt or the<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Tremere are utterly hated for eaten an Antediluvian, for the Giovanni it was Tuesday. I mean other than the Samedi and Harbingers of Skulls, does anyone really care about Cappadocious getting eaten? </div> </div> </div> I don't think people care about Saulot being eaten honestly. The Tremere aren't loathed for their crimes, they're loathed for the way they do business. The crimes are just extra justification for their hostility. The Giovanni are successful but not nearly as much as the Tremere: Necromancy isn't as marketable as thaumaturgy and it's considerably easier to master so the Giovanni can't dominate the market like the Tremere do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every clan is pulled into the great jyhad, except the Giovanni who are just left alone.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue are the greatest vampire bankers and CEO types, the Giovanni have entered chat and now own all the banks that the Ventrue work at.<br /> . </div> </div> </div>I agree completely, this is horseshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T03:12:22-07:00","id":1490499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490328#post1490328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Tremere are utterly hated for eaten an Antediluvian, for the Giovanni it was Tuesday. I mean other than the Samedi and Harbingers of Skulls, does anyone really care about Cappadocious getting eaten?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The cappadocians tended to be quite respected within kindred society, tending to fill a series of niche roles without being disruptive. They were pretty much the guy to go to for academic and Occult stuff. Their destruction personally inconvenienced a lot of important people in a way the salubris didn't , furthermore the cappadocians never had their reputation blackened so the extermination just comes across as worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T06:41:00-07:00","id":1490509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490499#post1490499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The cappadocians tended to be quite respected within kindred society, tending to fill a series of niche roles without being disruptive. They were pretty much the guy to go to for academic and Occult stuff. Their destruction personally inconvenienced a lot of important people in a way the salubris didn't , furthermore the cappadocians never had their reputation blackened so the extermination just comes across as worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have my doubts on this. &quot;Not being disruptive&quot; is an apt euphemism for &quot;being weak&quot;. Not especially helpful in-clan disciplines for feeding = low number of neonates = a clan without much organization centered around a few strong elders that are largely low key and support other elders because they struggle to compete themselves = useful guys to have around but if you want wisdom you're not losing out on much by ghouling a doctor instead + The Malkavians might be mad but I'd sooner deal with one of those over a guy obsessed with corpses.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni are a little too aggressive but they aren't more difficult to deal with compared to any other mainstream clan. They're -average- enemies and considerably better allies than the Capadocians. Their disciplines are better suited for neonates, their prefered necromancy paths are more suited to the modern day than the Capadocians. It's a good metaphor for big, modern, organized businesses outcompeting older, smaller and more traditional practices.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Giovanni get less flack than the Tremere because the Tremere are <i>perfect. </i> The Giovanni are divisive families brimming with internal conflict. The Tremere are a corporation. The Giovanni aren't much better than their competitors, the Tremere are the only large scale vampire organization built entirely around the fact that they're thaumaturges and so they can specialize where everyone else has to generalize. Thaumaturgy is in significantly more demand than necromancy. The Giovanni have a recognizeable vampiric weakness, the Tremere don't and are more inconvenienced by how shit-scared everyone is of them.<br /> <br /> All clans getting an equal start in city Hypothetiopolis: the Capadocians will fair as one of the worst, the Giovanni will be in the middle, the Tremere will be going strong. If you had to take the clan enmity flaw, you'd live best going up against the Capadocians, who would struggle to make your existence short or painful in comparison to other clans. Conversely if you could take clan friendship to go against an enemy, the worst choice would be capadocians...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T07:45:54-07:00","id":1490515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490509#post1490509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have my doubts on this. &quot;Not being disruptive&quot; is an apt euphemism for &quot;being weak&quot;. Not especially helpful in-clan disciplines for feeding = low number of neonates = a clan without much organization centered around a few strong elders that are largely low key and support other elders because they struggle to compete themselves = useful guys to have around but if you want wisdom you're not losing out on much by ghouling a doctor instead + The Malkavians might be mad but I'd sooner deal with one of those over a guy obsessed with corpses.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni are a little too aggressive but they aren't more difficult to deal with compared to any other mainstream clan. They're -average- enemies and considerably better allies than the Capadocians. Their disciplines are better suited for neonates, their prefered necromancy paths are more suited to the modern day than the Capadocians. It's a good metaphor for big, modern, organized businesses outcompeting older, smaller and more traditional practices.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Giovanni get less flack than the Tremere because the Tremere are <i>perfect. </i> The Giovanni are divisive families brimming with internal conflict. The Tremere are a corporation. The Giovanni aren't much better than their competitors, the Tremere are the only large scale vampire organization built entirely around the fact that they're thaumaturges and so they can specialize where everyone else has to generalize. Thaumaturgy is in significantly more demand than necromancy. The Giovanni have a recognizeable vampiric weakness, the Tremere don't and are more inconvenienced by how shit-scared everyone is of them.<br /> <br /> All clans getting an equal start in city Hypothetiopolis: the Capadocians will fair as one of the worst, the Giovanni will be in the middle, the Tremere will be going strong. If you had to take the clan enmity flaw, you'd live best going up against the Capadocians, who would struggle to make your existence short or painful in comparison to other clans. Conversely if you could take clan friendship to go against an enemy, the worst choice would be capadocians...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting arguement but not really backed by Canon, the cappadocians might be percieved as one of the weaker clans ( in hindsight) but they're overtly respected and established in da fluff prior to the purge. In contrast giovanni even we ignore the purge aspects are genrally considered weird incestuous scum who drive hard bargains for something most kindred find off putting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-17-2022, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T08:41:55-07:00","id":1490517,"title":"","content":"I don't know about that: The Necromancy Discipline states that it and those who practice it are considered gross in it's own writeup. Historically and Living people who worked with the dead were heavily stigmatized in that time period too (I know this applies to multiple cultures and I don't know who this didn't apply to, so I can't assume it universal but it is probably the common stance). You should also consider that Capadocians are one of the few dark age clans that really hated their founder; only the Nosferatu share that honour. It would be an unpopular stance since elders would want to encourage filial piety. <br /> <br /> Yeah, they're a &quot;high clan&quot; but I've wrote at length on why that little revised arbitration is an unsustainable and completely batshit distinction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T11:46:42-07:00","id":1490525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490517#post1490517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about that: The Necromancy Discipline states that it and those who practice it are considered gross in it's own writeup. Historically and Living people who worked with the dead were heavily stigmatized in that time period too (I know this applies to multiple cultures and I don't know who this didn't apply to, so I can't assume it universal but it is probably the common stance). You should also consider that Capadocians are one of the few dark age clans that really hated their founder; only the Nosferatu share that honour. It would be an unpopular stance since elders would want to encourage filial piety. <br /> <br /> Yeah, they're a &amp;quot;high clan&amp;quot; but I've wrote at length on why that little revised arbitration is an unsustainable and completely batshit distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>The cappadocians didn't really practice necromancy in either the wod or irl sense the mortis arts are built on decay, circumventing the curse or zombies. Its pretty bleak but not remarkably so compared to other clan disciplines such as obtenerbration, dement or viscitude. The giovanni by contrast practice more conventional necromancy with a necrophilia twist.<br /> <br /> I got the impression they were more terrified of their founded than hated him, simular to uncle aguie really.<br /> <br /> You have your reasoning certainly but most of issues you've mentioned are subjective ( I honestly think their disciplines are pretty good for example) and I could certainly comment on the clans merits as counterpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T13:48:14-07:00","id":1490539,"title":"","content":"Mortis=Necromancy, at least how it's used here. I know, the former just means &quot;death&quot; and the later means &quot;death divination&quot; but, y'know, we've been poluted by DnD ism's and it's a hard thing to change language from what's accepted. I'm still upset by V5 thinking Alchemy is all about novel magic potions but... yeah, it's semantics in this case. I would prefer to default to Mortis but, y'know, habits. <br /> <br /> <br /> I think Capadocians have great disciplines... when you've managed to make it after 20 years. Most vampires don't make it that far. Early mortis is utterly useless hunting. Auspex and Fortitude make a good character better but they don't make a mediocre character good. Potence, Dominate, Obfuscate, Animalism... these are powers that can make a mediocre character good and a good character thrive. You make a mistake hunting with just Fortitude and Auspex? Hot water; you'd be better off relying on blood buffs. You make a mistake with just two of the other six common disciplines, you're much more likely to recover while mitigating the consequences better. As a consequence the Capadocians need to be really careful with their selection and even then the attrition rates will be significantly harder since every feed is a struggle for the first few years. Sure, later on the in-clans are great. I'd rather have 5 auspex and 2 Potence than 5 Potence and 2 Auspex, but 2 Potence 0 Auspex is just so much better for new vampires than 2 Auspex 0 Potence, baring in mind that most clans get 3 common disciplines and the Cappadocians just have these two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T15:21:47-07:00","id":1490549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490328#post1490328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere are utterly hated for eaten an Antediluvian, for the Giovanni it was Tuesday. I mean other than the Samedi and Harbingers of Skulls, does anyone really care about Cappadocious getting eaten?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Giovanni were supposed to be the &quot;Devil Kindred&quot;. They were originally hunted and destroyed after their destruction of Cappadocious, and they survived only by making a deal with the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> But I do agree that the game has done a pretty bad job on two accounts in regards to this issue.<br /> <br /> First, what exactly were the obligations of the the Giovanni? This is one area where the original Giovanni Clanbook completely failed - it was merely an IC response that laughed at the Promise of 1528 and portrayed the Camarilla as suckers. That should obviously be discounted as an ignorant, puffing blowhard. If you make a desperate deal to save yourself from destruction, you pay dearly because you have no leverage. We can track back and assume some things - like the idea the Giovanni are only allowed to embrace 3 vampires per generation (and this is approved personally by Augustus) must have been part of the deal. But &quot;stay out of Kindred politics&quot; is so vague, it can be hard to determine what constitutes that, or what the punishment is for violation. In practice, I see most players (especially in LARP) ignore it entirely. In contrast, I put a lot of restrictions on the Giovanni in my chronicles and clearly present them as a second class &quot;citizen&quot; of any domain with many restrictions on them.<br /> <br /> Second, why would other vampires essentially let Giovanni wipe out the other Cappadocians? And why exactly did the Cappadocians lose? Shouldn't there be way more of them? It's not like they didn't have many active Methusalehs at the time. At least with the Salubri, we know the other clans hunted down the Salubri as well as the Tremere. But the Giovanni were by themselves and simply couldn't conduct a widescale hunt.<br /> <br /> Recently I picked up an old copy of the Giovanni Chronicles I - the Last Supper. It was the first time I read it. There's some interesting details in there that make this even more curious. First, it was the intention of the Founders of the Camarilla to include the Cappadocians in the Camarilla. As traditional allies of the Ventrue, this makes sense. Why abandon this simply because the diablerie was successful? Having an eighth clan would have strengthened them. Instead, the assumption seems to be that since Augustus is now 3rd generation, he rules the bloodline now and thus what he says goes. The Giovanni now &quot;control&quot; the Cappadocians, and thus determine the clan's internal policy. I don't think this really makes sense, and it is at odds with how the elders treated the diablerie of Lasombra and Tzimisce. But there's lots of problems with that sourcebook. It has some good ideas, but there's several things that make me go &quot;No, that's stupid.&quot;<br /> <br /> So in my chronicles, I go back to the old, old idea that the Black Death somehow affected some vampires too (the early game had some strange notions of various diseases affecting or even killing vampires themselves, but for the Black Death I say it had a supernatural component that allowed it to kill vampires too, it was not an ordinary disease), and state it was believed the Cappadocians (or their Founder) had something to do with it. So it made a lot of Kindred fear and dislike the Cappadocians. It also obviously made them a huge target for Anarchs. And the existence of the Feast of Folly meant there were a good amount of Cappadocian Anarchs too. Since Cappadocious was in a martyr mindset specifically wishing to be sacrificed in some kind of magical ritual, it is even possible he purposefully or inadvertently created such an impulse in other members of his clan, and that helped many of them be destroyed. So by the time the Camarilla managed to impose order and convened the Convention of Thorns, there wasn't much of the Cappadocians left. So rather than rally the few Cappadocians available and push the Giovanni into the new Sabbat, the Camarilla decided coming to terms with the Giovanni was preferable.<br /> <br /> But that didn't mean everyone didn't detest them. (At least the Sabbat was anathema to Kindred society. The Giovanni were those that &quot;got away&quot; with it, and sometimes you have to be in the same room with them. The Tremere were disliked, but their propaganda that Salubri were diabolists and soulsuckers worked so most vampires actually stopped hating them for that.) Or that many Camarilla members hoped the remaining Cappadocians would be able to rally and ultimately win the struggle for the clan (which in V5 they finally did).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T15:58:58-07:00","id":1490556,"title":"","content":"The purge would have been seen as an internal affair not much different from the usual Jyadd. . Unlike the Tremere usurpation, The Giovanni at that point were Capadocians, they'd been capadocians for hundreds of years. It would probably come down to who can win in a game of prestation, the Capadocian or the Giovanni.. As I've said, I don't think the Capadocians can compete. It's also pressing that the Capadocians aren't organized beyond the odd information exchange while the Giovanni very much are. Then there's all the Roads... <br /> <br /> A minor thing, but think the Cam higher ups would have been more agreeable to Capadocian extermination because the Capadocians suffer from the corpse look without having easy access to obfuscate. In addition, their style of Mortis is vulgar and significantly worse for the masquerade in comparison to their Giovanni counterparts. . <br /> <br /> The promise of 1520 is absurd and just seems like some BS the writers thought up at the 11th hour to justify why such a normal clan weren't corebook material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T16:10:07-07:00","id":1490558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490539#post1490539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortis=Necromancy, at least how it's used here. I know, the former just means &quot;death&quot; and the later means &quot;death divination&quot; but, y'know, we've been poluted by DnD ism's and it's a hard thing to change language from what's accepted. I'm still upset by V5 thinking Alchemy is all about novel magic potions but... yeah, it's semantics in this case. I would prefer to default to Mortis but, y'know, habits. <br /> <br /> <br /> I think Capadocians have great disciplines... when you've managed to make it after 20 years. Most vampires don't make it that far. Early mortis is utterly useless hunting. Auspex and Fortitude make a good character better but they don't make a mediocre character good. Potence, Dominate, Obfuscate, Animalism... these are powers that can make a mediocre character good and a good character thrive. You make a mistake hunting with just Fortitude and Auspex? Hot water; you'd be better off relying on blood buffs. You make a mistake with just two of the other six common disciplines, you're much more likely to recover while mitigating the consequences better. As a consequence the Capadocians need to be really careful with their selection and even then the attrition rates will be significantly harder since every feed is a struggle for the first few years. Sure, later on the in-clans are great. I'd rather have 5 auspex and 2 Potence than 5 Potence and 2 Auspex, but 2 Potence 0 Auspex is just so much better for new vampires than 2 Auspex 0 Potence, baring in mind that most clans get 3 common disciplines and the Cappadocians just have these two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Early mortis is actually pretty good for general vampire antics da:vampire. You have a ritual designed to refine more blood from corpses and two of the 3 paths start with respectively a buff/camouflage and a way of Destroying bodies quickly and efficiently When combined with Fortitude and auspex Cappadocians are natural at carrion feeding, better than giovanni in fact which is ironic because the giovanni clan flaw mean the dead are probably a better option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-17-2022, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T16:26:00-07:00","id":1490559,"title":"","content":"The Giovanni can have a thriving Underworld operation, regularly trading with Wraiths. And that can bleed into the physical plane. Wraiths Arcanoi arent just simple minor stuff, wraiths are actually very capable, and there are MILLIONS of them if not BILLIONS.<br /> <br /> Relations between Wraiths and Giovanni can be extremely benefitial for both parties, and there's a lot that can be achieved with their help.<br /> <br /> Also, there are very little other clans can do against Wraiths, even if they can perceive them using Auspex, and that is even more potentialized due to the lack of occult knowledge regarding ghosts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T16:37:55-07:00","id":1490563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490558#post1490558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the giovanni clan flaw mean the dead are probably a better option.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are, which makes one wonder what V5 Hecata do when they simply refuse to drink from corpses due to flavor, or simply become too potent to drink from corpses. How do they prevent themselves from becoming wights in an edition where humanity is the only option? I find it hard to believe these ancients would accept an existence of utter asceticism where they carefully keep their blood potency low, yet it doesn't seem like they'd have any other option now.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T17:04:24-07:00","id":1490565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490563#post1490563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are, which makes one wonder what V5 Hecata do when they simply refuse to drink from corpses due to flavor, or simply become too potent to drink from corpses. How do they prevent themselves from becoming wights in an edition where humanity is the only option? I find it hard to believe these ancients would accept an existence of utter asceticism where they carefully keep their blood potency low, yet it doesn't seem like they'd have any other option now.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well oblivion cannot really replicate the powers of the cappadocians very well and genrally struggles beyond childer/early neonate in terms of play. This is really bad with hecata were oblivion and lack of Paths makes the historically grim elders unviable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-17-2022, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T07:54:16-07:00","id":1490611,"title":"","content":"More related to the OP's question<br /> My wraith knowledge is lacking:<br /> <i>Can</i> the Giovanni actually utilize the resources of the shadowlands? I understand you can take things into the shadowlands, but apart from a few rare and not especially useful artifacts that make it into the shadowlands of their own accord there's no method to take anything born of the shadowlands out, right? I've never heard of Giovanni using Stygian steel or building parts of their havens with ghost bricks. Apart from knowledge, what exactly is the economic value of this alternative dimension for those firmly rooted in the living world? I know on the Umbral side of things there's a few factories in various Wyrm and weaver realms that do produce a limited number of goods for the material world, but I don't know squat about the dark umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T08:36:09-07:00","id":1490617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490611#post1490611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Can</i> the Giovanni actually utilize the resources of the shadowlands? I understand you can take things into the shadowlands, but apart from a few rare and not especially useful artifacts that make it into the shadowlands of their own accord there's no method to take anything born of the shadowlands out, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can, although there is some effort involved, because Underworld stuff fades in the Skinlands. Some Wraiths (Proctors) can cache Relics in the Skinlands for a very limited amount of time, where they appear like any mundane object. That power doesn't work for Artifacts or moliated corpus, but soulforged stuff seems to be ok. On the vampire side, Ash Path allows for some inter-shroud shenannigans. There's a Level 5 Ritual (Grasp the Ghostly) that can summon Relics for about a year. Theoretically it is possible to create a 'reverse Relic' (called a Phylactery for confusing reasons), but that is something Mummies do with extra special rites. Mages can probably jury-rig something to a similar effect.<br /> All in all getting stuff from the Underworld into the Skinlands is a lot of effort for little return. Information is definitely the most useful commodity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T08:36:21-07:00","id":1490618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490611#post1490611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More related to the OP's question<br /> My wraith knowledge is lacking:<br /> <i>Can</i> the Giovanni actually utilize the resources of the shadowlands? I understand you can take things into the shadowlands, but apart from a few rare and not especially useful artifacts that make it into the shadowlands of their own accord there's no method to take anything born of the shadowlands out, right? I've never heard of Giovanni using Stygian steel or building parts of their havens with ghost bricks. Apart from knowledge, what exactly is the economic value of this alternative dimension for those firmly rooted in the living world? I know on the Umbral side of things there's a few factories in various Wyrm and weaver realms that do produce a limited number of goods for the material world, but I don't know squat about the dark umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, no. 99.9999% of everything in the Underworld is restricted to that place. Anything that is not is special, thus wont be just laying around in the next goblin market. Such items will be the creations of Mages, Charon or the Deathlords, The Lady of Fate, Anubis, Nhudri, Lazarus, Japhet or even Augustus himself, therefore those are rather unique.<br /> <br /> What Wraiths can do is related to their Arcanoi - and they are not as powerless outside of the Underworld as most people believe. The use of Arcanoi goes beyound being just mere spies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T19:19:26-07:00","id":1490672,"title":"","content":"Yeah, even if they mostly get tthings that can't leave the Underworld, simply being able to accumulate things there means being able to contract Wraith's services. If they're a presence there, then despite they being known for their power to enslave Wraiths their relations are probably more complex and generally less antagonistic. That means a whole 'nother splat they can deal with with no one else being aware of it.<br /> <br /> And even if bringing stuff from the Shadowlands is hard, it isn't necessarily useless. Even temporary things can be well used, specially if your enemies or marks don't know they're temporary. And again, it's a source almost no one else is even aware of, so from a Vampire perspective it is free for to explore. They have to deal with powerful natives, but not with home rivals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T20:17:58-07:00","id":1490674,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Giovanni couldn't directly take their wealth from the Underworld and bring it to the real world or vice versa. But they could use their accumulated wealth in the Underworld to make alliances, or hire the services of powerful wraiths or groups of wraiths who could use their powers to affect the real world. Likewise they could use their real world resources to affect the Underworld, either protecting or destroying the fetters that ghosts are bound to.<br /> <br /> &quot;Work with us. We know you don't like Richard across the street. Do what we want and we'll burn down the historical building that serves as his fetter, then purchase the land and repave it into a parking lot. But if you don't want to work with us, maybe Richard will and it could be your fetter that gets turned into a parking lot. It doesn't much matter to us which way this goes, but I imagine it matters to you. So think about it. But don't take too long because maybe Richard might make a decision before you do.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T03:30:00-07:00","id":1490693,"title":"","content":"I have my doubts that spending time with wraiths would be more beneficial than, say, focusing on the living to build mundane backgrounds. If the Giovanni could encourage arcanoi that made their wraiths stronger that would be great for them but I think it would require very significant investment and would increase the danger to them. Arcanos are relatively cheap: getting them to level 4 (where they get good) is 25xp. Several are useful in the material world: Inhabit, Materialize, Fatalism Puppetry, outrage, pandemonium, Mnemosynis... Wraiths could be like Pokemon. However, these more-useful powers are more restricted and more likely to bring one into conflict with the wraith hierarchy. Furthermore, Dominate and the blood bond make many of these wraith utilities somewhat redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-19-2022, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T04:47:26-07:00","id":1490697,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of things that might more beneficial than spending time dealing with wraith. But that doesn't mean vampires won't be dealing with wraiths.<br /> <br /> Spending time posting on RPG messages forums is probably a lot less beneficial than spending time doing other things, and yet here we are. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T06:13:15-07:00","id":1490704,"title":"","content":"It's not wasted time if you enjoyed the process. Either that or I'm trying to retain some human interaction through one of the only means available to me within my padded cell. <br /> <br /> Points in it's favour though: vampires really don't have much to do between midnight and dawn. The mortal world has gone to sleep and so there are fewer options to feed or compete for power and influence. Excluding social gatherings with other kindred and a little book keeping your options are to either entertain yourself, learn skills, or truck with otherworldy entities. Spending some of 02:00-05:00 on ghost micromanagement is more likely productive than whatever your average vampire is doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T08:22:05-07:00","id":1490712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490693#post1490693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have my doubts that spending time with wraiths would be more beneficial than, say, focusing on the living to build mundane backgrounds. If the Giovanni could encourage arcanoi that made their wraiths stronger that would be great for them but I think it would require very significant investment and would increase the danger to them. Arcanos are relatively cheap: getting them to level 4 (where they get good) is 25xp. Several are useful in the material world: Inhabit, Materialize, Fatalism Puppetry, outrage, pandemonium, Mnemosynis... Wraiths could be like Pokemon. However, these more-useful powers are more restricted and more likely to bring one into conflict with the wraith hierarchy. Furthermore, Dominate and the blood bond make many of these wraith utilities somewhat redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Giovanni (or other necros) relationship with Wraiths is a covert operation, and goes a lot less &quot;we enslave every wraith&quot; and more into covert cooperation (hidden from the &quot;authorities&quot; - aka Stygia or other dark kingdoms). But, despite that, there's still the enslaving of SOME wraiths (or Spectres). It is worth reminding that slavery IS more than just common in the Underworld, so I doubt any of the Ghost allies of the Giovanni would ever batch an eye over it - as long as they believe themselves not to become their next victims.<br /> <br /> There are benefits to that for the necros no matter what, even if Fatalism is redundant for a vamp with Presence or Mnemosis being sort of redundant for one with Dominate. First of, the necro wont need to look another in the eyes if his ghost pal uses Mnemosis on his behalf. There's also plausible deniability. It's gonna be a lot harder to connect Ghostly activity to a necromancer than if the vamp were using ghouls and/or neonates to target a rival - that is, if the victim can identify that he is been targeted by ghosts at all. Nobody can accuse you of using Dominate to erase memories if you have the perfect alibi of being in a party at the Elysium.<br /> <br /> On top of that, despite some level of redundancy, Arcanoi and Disciplines are NOT exact matches. Thus, this means that there are some effects that go beyond what vampires can commonly do - and on top of that, those would be largely unknow to the vast majority of non necromancers.<br /> <br /> Yes, there is an additional difficulty with &quot;collecting&quot; Wraiths with specially useful Arcanoi - particularlly because the &quot;ghost authorities&quot; dislike them.<br /> <br /> But... Even that also have it's pros. Practitioners of those, and even more, guild members of hunted guilds, would be a lot more willing to &quot;pay for protection&quot; - to anyone capable of protecting them.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni can greatly help in that - being mobsters in both the Skinlands and the Shadowlands. Those Wraiths could count on Giovanni help for protection, in exchange for services, in a truly mutually benefitial relation.<br /> <br /> And that's not all. Necros probably wouldnt have much trouble working with SPECTRES too. At least, not problems related with morality. Necros need not worry about Spectres trying to &quot;convert&quot; or throw them in Oblivion (well, at least as long as they remain in the right side of the Shroud).<br /> <br /> Giovanni wont be world-shakers in the Underworld, but they certanly are a powerful criminal gang.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T20:43:00-07:00","id":1490751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490704#post1490704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not wasted time if</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the core of the question.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni practice Necromancy and deal with Wraiths.<br /> <br /> If other means of accruing power are more effective is irrelevant, Necromancy is already what they're doing.<br /> <br /> Using their time and focus to be Necromancers and then ignoring it altogether to build up power by other means, <b>that</b> is a waste of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T06:44:54-07:00","id":1490784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490295-the-economics-of-necromancy?p=1490751#post1490751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the core of the question.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni practice Necromancy and deal with Wraiths.<br /> <br /> If other means of accruing power are more effective is irrelevant, Necromancy is already what they're doing.<br /> <br /> Using their time and focus to be Necromancers and then ignoring it altogether to build up power by other means, <b>that</b> is a waste of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a little... <br /> Ignoring necromancer powers you've spent a long time building up is wasting those powers, but if your choice is between raising a third ghost and increasing your power by 10% or spending that time toadying up with an ally that could increase the security of your position twice over then the choice is obvious. Wraiths are diminishing returns: one ghost is a massive advantage over those without, the second ghost is more advantageous when you're against another necromancer or against multiple opponents but ultimately it's maybe 90% the effort of the first ghost with 60% of the use. Allies, resources... these are backgrounds that are providing an exponential increase power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T07:35:56-07:00","id":1490790,"title":"","content":"I don't know if I agree with that. Ghosts have a wide range of Arcanoi, enough that investing heavily in ghosts in order to have broad access to those Arcanoi is a viable strategy. There are wraiths that can possess computers, or wraiths who can punch across the Shroud and kill people in the living world, or wraiths that can possess people, or wraiths that can instantly heal the living, or wraiths that can swap the minds/souls of mortals. Any of those could be incredibly useful.<br /> <br /> Sure in theory if you have Schrodinger's Wraith who has access to every Arcanoi then you'd start to run into diminishing returns if you keep looking to recruit more wraiths who can only do the same things as the one you already recruited. But realistically you're not going to be able to recruit a single wraith who has every Arcanoi you'd like to have access to, so making deals with multiple wraiths may become necessary if you want access to the various abilities that wraiths can perform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T07:52:54-07:00","id":1490791,"title":"","content":"Arcanoi are useful and interesting powers but I'd still say 80% of why you'd want a ghost is for the invisible, intangible spy. For other purposes finding a mortal and applying Money/Blood/Dominate/Blackmail is more cost effective. Necromancy has a handful of really good locating spells (+hand of glory) which can be used to direct mortal agents/ghouls","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T09:24:20-07:00","id":1490801,"title":"","content":"Again, the point is that the character is a Necromancer, first and foremost. While they can get plenty benefits from diversifying sources of influence and power whenever they can, most of the time they're dealing with ghosts and the Underworld. Building up a power base in the Underworld helps their primary concern and also increase their overall power. Making pacts with the Hierarchy helps their primary concern and also increase their overall power.<br /> <br /> My point is, when you put it as &quot;I have my doubts that spending time with wraiths would be more beneficial than, say, focusing on the living to build mundane backgrounds&quot;, you're ignoring that this character <b>will</b> spend time with wraiths regardless. They'll do so because they're <b>dedicated</b> Necromancers (as opposed to a business-focused clan member that just happens to also have some dots in <b>Necromancy</b>).<br /> <br /> However better it is to built up power in the material world, this character's whole shtick, their goal in life, is to build up necromantic knowledge and power. For <b>this character</b>, amassing mundane power is a distraction, and playing against their strengths, while power within the Underworld is at hand and plenty useful for their actual purposes. They may later use this power and those connections to help an ally that will take care of the mundane power better than they would (which is the benefit of having both types within the same tight-knit clan).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}